OL,3,GNEWSAWorld's only flying Seafire XVII
OL,4,Areturns home
OL,5,
OL,6,FA rare Naval Spitfire - the only flying
OL,7,FSeafire XVII in the world - has
OL,8,Freturned home close to where it was
OL,9,Fbuilt in Somerset.
OL,11,FDescribed as the "big brother of the
OL,12,FSpitfire", the single-seater fighter
OL,13,Fplane was modified by the Royal Navy to
OL,14,Foperate from aircraft carriers during
OL,15,FWorld War Two.
OL,17,FBuilt by Westlands in Yeovil in 1946,
OL,18,Fthe Seafire has now joined the Navy
OL,19,FWings charity collection at nearby RNAS
OL,20,FYeovilton after undergoing three years
OL,21,Fof repairs.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
